06509021669626,-9.536738616588991e-07,-0.0010380124440416694,-2.3007127310847864e-05],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,729,400,69,2075,15087,67901,198,78045,69,955,2075,593,284,220,21,87,481,220,17,15,15,20,59,60,1958,678,1931,5109,400,87,2418,220,2619,6724,458,7546,400,77,3,1741,429,400,69,1445,8,284,220,21,77,481,220,17,15,15,20,2418,220,7379,400,77,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe function $f(x)$ satisfies\n\\[f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005\\]for all real numbers $x.$  There exists an integer $n$ such that $f(n) = 6n - 2005.$  Find $n.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9b5dd2453e33d710694bea7aa506aba5107605ce80a548140b46970ff00f156c"},"seconds":53.331358194351196,"seed":699673786107763127,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to find an integer \\( n \\) such that \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\) given the functional equation \\( f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005 \\).\n\n**Step 1: Analyze the functional equation.**\n\nGiven:\n\\[ f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005 \\]\n\n**Step 2: Consider the form of \\( f(x) \\).**\n\nAssume \\( f(x) = ax + b \\). We need to determine the values of \\( a \\) and \\( b \\). Substitute \\( f(x) = ax + b \\) into the functional equation:\n\\[ f(f(x)) = f(ax + b) \\]\n\\[ f(ax + b) = a(ax + b) + b = a^2x + ab + b \\]\n\nGiven \\( f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005 \\), we equate:\n\\[ a^2x + ab + b = 6x - 2005 \\]\n\nThis gives us two equations by comparing coefficients:\n1. \\( a^2 = 6 \\)\n2. \\( ab + b = -2005 \\)\n\n**Step 3: Solve for \\( a \\) and \\( b \\).**\n\nFrom \\( a^2 = 6 \\), we get:\n\\[ a = \\sqrt{6} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad a = -\\sqrt{6} \\]\n\n**Step 4: Determine \\( b \\) for each value of \\( a \\).**\n\nFor \\( a = \\sqrt{6} \\):\n\\[ (\\sqrt{6})b + b = -2005 \\]\n\\[ b(\\sqrt{6} + 1) = -2005 \\]\n\\[ b = \\frac{-2005}{\\sqrt{6} + 1} \\]\n\nFor \\( a = -\\sqrt{6} \\):\n\\[ (-\\sqrt{6})b + b = -2005 \\]\n\\[ b(-\\sqrt{6} + 1) = -2005 \\]\n\\[ b = \\frac{-2005}{-\\sqrt{6} + 1} \\]\n\n**Step 5: Check for integer solutions.**\n\nGiven \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\), we need \\( f(x) = 6x - 2005 \\) to be consistent with the form \\( f(x) = ax + b \\).\n\nIf \\( f(x) = 6x - 2005 \\), then:\n\\[ f(f(x)) = f(6x - 2005) = 6(6x - 2005) - 2005 = 36x - 12030 - 2005 = 36x - 14035 \\]\n\nHowever, this does not match \\( 6x - 2005 \\). Thus, we need to find \\( n \\) such that \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\).\n\n**Step 6: Use the given condition \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\).**\n\nIf \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\), then:\n\\[ f(f(n)) = f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005 \\]\n\nSince \\( f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005 \\), we set \\( x = n \\):\n\\[ f(f(n)) = 6n - 2005 \\]\n\nThus, \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\) is consistent with the functional equation. Therefore, the integer \\( n \\) that satisfies \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{2005} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2005}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
